  "hypotheses": [
    "A hard process exit after inserting an uncommitted snapshot cannot expose a partial or advanced epoch after the SQLite authority is reopened.",
    "Two publishers using the same current snapshot hash have exactly one CAS winner and produce a strictly monotonic committed epoch sequence.",
    "Within the component HMAC and host-boot boundary, signature, payload, stale-snapshot, minimum-epoch, and boot replay failures are rejected before launch authorization.",
    "Without an external monotonic anchor, deleting the newest row leaves an earlier correctly signed SQLite state acceptable even when the inode and store UUID remain unchanged."
  ],
